{
 "comment": "loans_interest #779 Phase A, s.194A, a firm: a two-sided voucher carrying interest that takes the interest over the threshold (Threshold Loan) or back under it (Reverse Loan): whether it crosses is not computed; over the threshold either way with no TDS anywhere, the s.194A finding stays and names the listed interest (Default Loan); TDS on a two-sided voucher over the threshold, coverage not computed and the TDS may be on it (Seen Loan), and under it, coverage still reads not computed but no s.194A finding is raised (Under Loan); a deduction with the credit and a duplicate deducted and reversed, covered by amount, not by date (Dated Loan); the Threshold shape on a lender exempt from s.194A (Insurer Loan). Seen and Under Loan carry TDS on a listed voucher, where LOAN-1 names the TDS (the reference's pinned OQ-2).",
